IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ucpr-dates`

-- Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 1999 (Qld) -- the rules a person bringing a claim meets, by chapter, with one
-- regulative rule (rr 547 and 550, the personal injury statements).
-- Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the version in force from 29 October
-- 2026). (c) The State of Queensland, CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Throughout: the court "may, at any time, extend a time set under these rules or by order" (r 7(1)), so every last
-- day is the last day unless the court extends it. "Plaintiff" includes a party who files a counterclaim or a third
-- party notice (Schedule 3); the seat is the plaintiff who brings the claim.

§ `Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 1999 -- the claimant's rules`

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`yes or no` b MEANS
    IF b
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Chapter 2, Part 3 -- the claim (r 24)`

-- r 24(1): "A claim remains in force for 1 year starting on the day it is filed." The filing day is the first day, so
-- the last day is the day before the first anniversary.
GIVEN `the day the claim was filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 24(1) -- the last day my claim is in force` `the day the claim was filed` MEANS
    `the day n days before` (`the nth anniversary of` `the day the claim was filed` 1) 1

-- r 24(6): "for any time limit (including a limitation period), a claim that is renewed is taken to have started on the
-- day the claim was originally filed."
GIVEN `the day the claim was originally filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 24(6) -- the day my renewed claim is taken to have started` `the day the claim was originally filed` MEANS
    `the day the claim was originally filed`

DECLARE `Renewal answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: rule 24(2) renews only a claim not yet served on the defendant`
    `no: the registrar is not satisfied of reasonable efforts to serve or another good reason`
    `yes: the registrar may renew it for up to 1 year without the court's leave`
    `the registrar may renew it without leave only up to the day before the fifth anniversary; a longer period needs the court's leave`
    `only with the court's leave: the whole renewal period falls on or after the fifth anniversary`

-- r 24(2)-(4). (2) "If the claim has not been served on a defendant and the registrar is satisfied that reasonable
-- efforts have been made to serve the defendant or that there is another good reason to renew the claim, the registrar
-- may renew the claim for further periods, of not more than 1 year at a time, starting on the day after the claim would
-- otherwise end." (3) whether or not in force. (4) "the court's leave must be obtained before a claim may be renewed for
-- a period any part of which falls on or after the fifth anniversary of the day on which the claim was originally
-- filed." The registrar's satisfaction is an input. A full year of renewal runs from its first day to the day before
-- the anniversary of that day.
GIVEN `the day the claim was originally filed` IS A DATE, `the day the claim would otherwise end` IS A DATE,
      `the claim has been served on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN, `the registrar is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Renewal answer`
`r 24(2)-(4) -- can my claim be renewed` `the day the claim was originally filed` `the day the claim would otherwise end` `the claim has been served on the defendant` `the registrar is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the claim has been served on the defendant`
    THEN `no: rule 24(2) renews only a claim not yet served on the defendant`
    ELSE IF (NOT `the registrar is satisfied`)
         THEN `no: the registrar is not satisfied of reasonable efforts to serve or another good reason`
         ELSE IF (NOT (`is after` `the fifth anniversary` `the last day of a full renewal`))
              THEN IF `is after` `the fifth anniversary` `the first day of renewal`
                   THEN `the registrar may renew it without leave only up to the day before the fifth anniversary; a longer period needs the court's leave`
                   ELSE `only with the court's leave: the whole renewal period falls on or after the fifth anniversary`
              ELSE `yes: the registrar may renew it for up to 1 year without the court's leave`
    WHERE
        `the fifth anniversary` MEANS `the nth anniversary of` `the day the claim was originally filed` 5
        `the first day of renewal` MEANS `the day n days after` `the day the claim would otherwise end` 1
        `the last day of a full renewal` MEANS `the day n days before` (`the nth anniversary of` `the first day of renewal` 1) 1

§§ `Chapter 5 and Chapter 9, Part 1 -- the notice of intention to defend and default judgment (rr 137, 281-288)`

-- r 137(1): "a notice of intention to defend must be filed within 28 days after the day the claim is served." r 137(2):
-- where the Service and Execution of Process Act 1992 (Cwlth) applies, the time that Act limits (not deposited).
GIVEN `the day the claim was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 137 -- the last day for the notice of intention to defend` `the day the claim was served` MEANS
    `the last day of n days after` `the day the claim was served` 28

DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `a debt or liquidated demand`
    `unliquidated damages`
    `detention of goods only`
    `recovery of possession of land only`
    `two or more of those four kinds and nothing else`
    `any other claim`

DECLARE `Default judgment answer` IS ONE OF
    `not under these rules: the Service and Execution of Process Act 1992 (Cwlth) sets the time`
    `not yet: the 28 days for a notice of intention to defend have not ended`
    `no: the defendant has filed a notice of intention to defend`
    `not yet: I must first prove service of the claim`
    `yes: I can file a request for judgment for not more than the amount claimed, interest and costs, given by a registrar (r 283)`
    `yes: I can file a request for judgment conditional on the assessment of damages, and costs (r 284)`
    `yes: I can file a request for judgment for the return or value of the goods (r 285)`
    `yes: I can file a request for judgment for possession of the land and costs (r 286)`
    `no: rule 286 gives no judgment for delivery of possession under a mortgage; I must apply to the court (r 288)`
    `yes: I can request judgment on each claim as if it were my only claim (r 287)`
    `I must apply to the court for the judgment it considers justified on the pleadings (r 288)`

-- Chapter 9, Part 1, Division 2. r 281(1): the division "applies if a defendant ... has not filed a notice of intention
-- to defend and the time allowed under rule 137 to file the notice has ended" -- the time ends with its last day, so a
-- request on the 29th day after service is the first in time. r 138: a notice can be filed "at any time before
-- judgment", so a late notice filed before the request takes the case out of the division. r 282: "A plaintiff must
-- prove service ... before judgment may be given". rr 283-288 by the kind of claim. r 281(2) (a conditional notice
-- that becomes unconditional without a defence) is not encoded.
GIVEN `the day the claim was served` IS A DATE, `the day I request judgment` IS A DATE,
      `the Service and Execution of Process Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a notice of intention to defend has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN, `I can prove service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `my claim` IS A `Kind of claim`, `possession is claimed under a mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Default judgment answer`
`rr 281-288 -- can I get default judgment` `the day the claim was served` `the day I request judgment` `the Service and Execution of Process Act applies` `a notice of intention to defend has been filed` `I can prove service` `my claim` `possession is claimed under a mortgage` MEANS
    IF `the Service and Execution of Process Act applies`
    THEN `not under these rules: the Service and Execution of Process Act 1992 (Cwlth) sets the time`
    ELSE IF `a notice of intention to defend has been filed`
         THEN `no: the defendant has filed a notice of intention to defend`
         ELSE IF (NOT (`is after` `the day I request judgment` (`r 137 -- the last day for the notice of intention to defend` `the day the claim was served`)))
              THEN `not yet: the 28 days for a notice of intention to defend have not ended`
              ELSE IF (NOT `I can prove service`)
                   THEN `not yet: I must first prove service of the claim`
                   ELSE CONSIDER `my claim`
                        WHEN `a debt or liquidated demand` THEN `yes: I can file a request for judgment for not more than the amount claimed, interest and costs, given by a registrar (r 283)`
                        WHEN `unliquidated damages` THEN `yes: I can file a request for judgment conditional on the assessment of damages, and costs (r 284)`
                        WHEN `detention of goods only` THEN `yes: I can file a request for judgment for the return or value of the goods (r 285)`
                        WHEN `recovery of possession of land only` THEN
                            IF `possession is claimed under a mortgage`
                            THEN `no: rule 286 gives no judgment for delivery of possession under a mortgage; I must apply to the court (r 288)`
                            ELSE `yes: I can file a request for judgment for possession of the land and costs (r 286)`
                        WHEN `two or more of those four kinds and nothing else` THEN `yes: I can request judgment on each claim as if it were my only claim (r 287)`
                        WHEN `any other claim` THEN `I must apply to the court for the judgment it considers justified on the pleadings (r 288)`

DECLARE `Court` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court or the District Court`
    `a Magistrates Court`

-- r 283(2)(b): with a default judgment for a debt, "(i) costs for issuing the claim; (ii) costs for obtaining judgment;
-- (iii) any other fees and payments, to the extent they have been reasonably incurred and paid". r 694: "the registrar
-- must fix the costs in accordance with the prescribed scale". Schedule 1 (Supreme and District Courts), fixed cost
-- items 19 ($2,123.00) and 20 ($558.00). Schedule 2 (Magistrates Courts), Part 2 items 1 (instructions to sue) and 4
-- (obtaining judgment by default), in the column for the amount (r 691(3): the amount recovered on the standard basis):
-- A $2,500 or under 454.55 + 119.95; B over $2,500 to $5,000 858.55 + 200.15; C over $5,000 to $20,000 1,343.00 +
-- 303.40; D over $20,000 to $50,000 1,491.00 + 333.10. Over $50,000, Part 3 has no fixed items: NOTHING (the registrar
-- or a costs assessor decides). Item 1 is read as "costs for issuing the claim" (fork F6).
GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`, `the amount of the judgment` IS A NUMBER, `fees and payments reasonably incurred and paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`r 283(2)(b) -- the fixed costs on my default judgment` `the court` `the amount of the judgment` `fees and payments reasonably incurred and paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the court`
    WHEN `the Supreme Court or the District Court` THEN JUST (2123 PLUS 558 PLUS `fees and payments reasonably incurred and paid`)
    WHEN `a Magistrates Court` THEN
        IF `the amount of the judgment` AT MOST 2500
        THEN JUST (454.55 PLUS 119.95 PLUS `fees and payments reasonably incurred and paid`)
        ELSE IF `the amount of the judgment` AT MOST 5000
             THEN JUST (858.55 PLUS 200.15 PLUS `fees and payments reasonably incurred and paid`)
             ELSE IF `the amount of the judgment` AT MOST 20000
                  THEN JUST (1343 PLUS 303.40 PLUS `fees and payments reasonably incurred and paid`)
                  ELSE IF `the amount of the judgment` AT MOST 50000
                       THEN JUST (1491 PLUS 333.10 PLUS `fees and payments reasonably incurred and paid`)
                       ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Chapter 6 -- pleadings (rr 164, 169, 189)`

-- r 164(2): "any reply must be filed and served within 14 days after the day of the service of the defence or answer
-- to counterclaim."
GIVEN `the day the defence was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 164(2) -- the last day for my reply` `the day the defence was served` MEANS
    `the last day of n days after` `the day the defence was served` 14

-- r 164(1): an answer to counterclaim within "(a) 14 days after the day the counterclaim is served; or (b) if the
-- defendant to the counterclaim is not a party to the original proceeding, 28 days".
GIVEN `the day the counterclaim was served` IS A DATE, `I was a party to the original proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`r 164(1) -- the last day for my answer to counterclaim` `the day the counterclaim was served` `I was a party to the original proceeding` MEANS
    IF `I was a party to the original proceeding`
    THEN `the last day of n days after` `the day the counterclaim was served` 14
    ELSE `the last day of n days after` `the day the counterclaim was served` 28

-- r 169: "The pleadings ... close-- (a) if a pleading is served after the defence or answer to a counterclaim--on
-- service of the pleading; or (b) otherwise--14 days after service of the defence." Under (a), the first pleading
-- served after the defence.
GIVEN `the day the defence was served` IS A DATE, `a pleading was served after the defence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day that pleading was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 169 -- the day the pleadings close` `the day the defence was served` `a pleading was served after the defence` `the day that pleading was served` MEANS
    IF `a pleading was served after the defence`
    THEN `the day that pleading was served`
    ELSE `the day n days after` `the day the defence was served` 14

DECLARE `Notice to admit answer` IS ONE OF
    `not yet: the 14 days for a disputing notice have not ended`
    `no: the other party served a notice disputing it within 14 days`
    `yes: the other party is taken to admit it, for this proceeding only, unless the court gives leave to withdraw`

-- r 189(2): "If the other party does not, within 14 days, serve a notice on the first party disputing the fact or the
-- authenticity of the document, the other party is taken to admit" it. (3): withdrawal only with the court's leave.
-- (4): a party who disputes and is proved wrong "must pay the costs of proof, unless the court otherwise orders".
GIVEN `the day my notice to admit was served` IS A DATE, `a disputing notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day the disputing notice was served` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice to admit answer`
`r 189 -- is the other party taken to admit` `the day my notice to admit was served` `a disputing notice was served` `the day the disputing notice was served` `today` MEANS
    IF `a disputing notice was served` AND `is on or before` `the day the disputing notice was served` `the last day` AND `is on or before` `the day the disputing notice was served` `today`
    THEN `no: the other party served a notice disputing it within 14 days`
    ELSE IF `is on or before` `today` `the last day`
         THEN `not yet: the 14 days for a disputing notice have not ended`
         ELSE `yes: the other party is taken to admit it, for this proceeding only, unless the court gives leave to withdraw`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the last day of n days after` `the day my notice to admit was served` 14

§§ `Chapter 7 -- disclosure (r 214)`

-- r 214(2): lists of documents. "(a) if an order for disclosure is made before the close of pleadings--the times stated
-- in the order; ... (e) otherwise--within 28 days after the close of pleadings." Heads (b) and (c) are not encoded;
-- (a) points to the order, outside the sources: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the day the pleadings closed` IS A DATE, `an order for disclosure was made before the close of pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`r 214(2) -- the last day for my list of documents` `the day the pleadings closed` `an order for disclosure was made before the close of pleadings` MEANS
    IF `an order for disclosure was made before the close of pleadings`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the last day of n days after` `the day the pleadings closed` 28)

-- r 214(2)(d): a document that comes into my possession or control, or is located, after those times: "within 7 days
-- after the occasion happens". r 214(3): copies requested "must be delivered within 14 days after the request".
GIVEN `the day I found or got the document` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 214(2)(d) -- the last day to disclose a later document` `the day I found or got the document` MEANS
    `the last day of n days after` `the day I found or got the document` 7

GIVEN `the day copies were requested` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 214(3) -- the last day to deliver requested copies` `the day copies were requested` MEANS
    `the last day of n days after` `the day copies were requested` 14

§§ `Chapter 14, Part 2 -- personal injury and fatal accidents (rr 545-558)`

DECLARE `Statement answer` IS ONE OF
    `Part 2 of Chapter 14 does not apply: the proceeding is not for damages for personal injury or death`
    `no further statement is needed: compliance with Part 2 was waived by written notice (r 546)`
    `serve it within 28 days after the close of pleadings, and before any request for trial date is filed`

-- r 545(1): "This part applies to a proceeding for damages for personal injury or death." r 546: "A party may, by
-- written notice, waive further compliance with this part." r 547(1)-(2): "The plaintiff must serve on the defendant a
-- written statement of loss and damage, signed by the plaintiff, within 28 days after the close of pleadings" and
-- "before a request for trial date is filed".
GIVEN `my claim is for damages for personal injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN, `the defendant waived compliance in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Statement answer`
`rr 545-547 -- must I serve a statement of loss and damage` `my claim is for damages for personal injury or death` `the defendant waived compliance in writing` MEANS
    IF (NOT `my claim is for damages for personal injury or death`)
    THEN `Part 2 of Chapter 14 does not apply: the proceeding is not for damages for personal injury or death`
    ELSE IF `the defendant waived compliance in writing`
         THEN `no further statement is needed: compliance with Part 2 was waived by written notice (r 546)`
         ELSE `serve it within 28 days after the close of pleadings, and before any request for trial date is filed`

GIVEN `the day the pleadings closed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 547(1) -- the last day for my statement of loss and damage` `the day the pleadings closed` MEANS
    `the last day of n days after` `the day the pleadings closed` 28

-- r 550(2): the defendant's statement of expert and economic evidence "must be served within 28 days after the
-- defendant is served with the plaintiff's statement of loss and damage, but before a request for trial date is filed".
GIVEN `the day my statement was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 550(2) -- the last day for the defendant's statement` `the day my statement was served` MEANS
    `the last day of n days after` `the day my statement was served` 28

DECLARE `Statement party` IS ONE OF `the plaintiff`, `the defendant`
DECLARE `Statement action` IS ONE OF
    `serve a statement of loss and damage`
    `serve a statement of expert and economic evidence`

-- rr 547(1) and 550(2) as a chain of duties: the plaintiff's statement within 28 days after the close of pleadings,
-- HENCE the defendant's within 28 days after being served with it. A breach is not itself sanctioned by Part 2; r 557
-- lets the court take a failure into account in costs, and rr 548(4) and 551(4) limit evidence not identified at
-- trial. Counted in days from the close of pleadings.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Statement party` `Statement action`
`rr 547, 550 -- the personal injury statements` MEANS
    PARTY `the plaintiff`
    MUST `serve a statement of loss and damage`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE
        PARTY `the defendant`
        MUST `serve a statement of expert and economic evidence`
        WITHIN 28
        LEST BREACH BY `the defendant` BECAUSE "no statement of expert and economic evidence within 28 days after service of the plaintiff's statement of loss and damage (r 550(2)); the court may take this into account in costs (r 557)"
    LEST BREACH BY `the plaintiff` BECAUSE "no statement of loss and damage within 28 days after the close of pleadings (r 547(1)); the court may take this into account in costs (r 557)"

DECLARE `Statements answer` IS ONE OF
    `I was late with my statement of loss and damage`
    `the defendant was late with its statement of expert and economic evidence`
    `both statements were served in time`
    `my statement was in time and the defendant's 28 days are still running`

-- Runs the chain on plain dates, as at today. Not exported.
GIVEN `the day the pleadings closed` IS A DATE, `the day my statement was served` IS A DATE,
      `the defendant has served its statement` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day the defendant's statement was served` IS A DATE,
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Statements answer`
`rr 547, 550 -- were the statements in time` `the day the pleadings closed` `the day my statement was served` `the defendant has served its statement` `the day the defendant's statement was served` `today` MEANS
    IF `days from` `the day the pleadings closed` `the day my statement was served` GREATER THAN 28
    THEN `I was late with my statement of loss and damage`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `rr 547, 550 -- the personal injury statements` 0 `the events`
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `both statements were served in time`
         OTHERWISE
             IF `defendant still in time`
             THEN `my statement was in time and the defendant's 28 days are still running`
             ELSE `the defendant was late with its statement of expert and economic evidence`
    WHERE
        `day mine` MEANS `days from` `the day the pleadings closed` `the day my statement was served`
        `defendant served by today` MEANS `the defendant has served its statement` AND `is on or before` `the day the defendant's statement was served` `today`
        `defendant still in time` MEANS
            (NOT `defendant served by today`)
            AND `is on or before` `today` (`r 550(2) -- the last day for the defendant's statement` `the day my statement was served`)
        `day theirs` MEANS
            IF `defendant served by today`
            THEN `days from` `the day the pleadings closed` `the day the defendant's statement was served`
            ELSE `days from` `the day the pleadings closed` `today` PLUS 1000
        `the events` MEANS
            LIST (EVENT `the plaintiff` `serve a statement of loss and damage` `day mine`),
                 (EVENT `the defendant` `serve a statement of expert and economic evidence` `day theirs`),
                 (WAITUNTIL (`day theirs` PLUS 1))

-- r 558(2): where an assessment of damages is ordered before the plaintiff complies with Part 2 and the defendant has an
-- address for service, the plaintiff must serve a full statement "at least 21 days before the date set for the
-- assessment". (4): a defendant who intends to appear "must serve ... 7 days before the date set". (1): not in the
-- Magistrates Court. Read as the act's own day being the 21st (7th) day before, the assessment day not counted (fork F2).
GIVEN `the day set for the assessment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 558(2) -- the last day for my statement before an assessment` `the day set for the assessment` MEANS
    `the last day at least n days before` `the day set for the assessment` 21

GIVEN `the day set for the assessment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 558(4) -- the day for the defendant's statement before an assessment` `the day set for the assessment` MEANS
    `the last day at least n days before` `the day set for the assessment` 7

§§ `Chapter 3 -- a claimant under a legal incapacity (rr 98, 359)`

-- r 98(1): "A settlement or compromise of a proceeding in which a party is a person under a legal incapacity is
-- ineffective unless it is approved by the court or the public trustee acting under the Public Trustee Act 1978,
-- section 59." r 359(2): an offer made or accepted by such a party "is not binding on the party unless it is approved"
-- the same way. Both "unless": a flat no without approval.
GIVEN `I am a person under a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court or the public trustee approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`rr 98, 359 -- my settlement is binding on me` `I am a person under a legal incapacity` `the court or the public trustee approved it` MEANS
    IF `I am a person under a legal incapacity`
    THEN `yes or no` `the court or the public trustee approved it`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Chapter 9, Part 3 -- discontinuance (rr 303, 304, 307)`

DECLARE `Discontinuance answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I can discontinue by filing a notice and serving it on the other parties`
    `only with the court's leave or the consent of the other parties`
    `only with the court's leave, because I represent another person`

-- r 303(1): "A party who represents another person in a proceeding may discontinue or withdraw only with the court's
-- leave." r 304(1): before being served with "the first defence of any defendant"; (2) after it, "only with the court's
-- leave or the consent of the other parties"; (3) "if there is more than 1 plaintiff ..., or a counterclaim against a
-- plaintiff", the same. r 309(1): without leave, by filing a notice and serving it.
GIVEN `I represent another person` IS A BOOLEAN, `I have been served with the first defence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `there is more than one plaintiff` IS A BOOLEAN, `there is a counterclaim against me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Discontinuance answer`
`rr 303, 304 -- can I discontinue without leave` `I represent another person` `I have been served with the first defence` `there is more than one plaintiff` `there is a counterclaim against me` MEANS
    IF `I represent another person`
    THEN `only with the court's leave, because I represent another person`
    ELSE IF `I have been served with the first defence` OR `there is more than one plaintiff` OR `there is a counterclaim against me`
         THEN `only with the court's leave or the consent of the other parties`
         ELSE `yes: I can discontinue by filing a notice and serving it on the other parties`

DECLARE `Discontinuance costs` IS ONE OF
    `I must pay the defendant's costs up to the discontinuance and any costs it causes another party`
    `whatever costs order the court considers appropriate`

-- r 307: "(1) A party who discontinues or withdraws is liable to pay-- (a) the costs of the party to whom the
-- discontinuance ... relates up to the discontinuance ...; and (b) the costs of another party or parties caused by the
-- discontinuance ... (2) If a party discontinues or withdraws with the court's leave, the court may make the order for
-- costs it considers appropriate."
GIVEN `I discontinue with the court's leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Discontinuance costs`
`r 307 -- the costs if I discontinue` `I discontinue with the court's leave` MEANS
    IF `I discontinue with the court's leave`
    THEN `whatever costs order the court considers appropriate`
    ELSE `I must pay the defendant's costs up to the discontinuance and any costs it causes another party`

§§ `Chapter 9, Part 5 -- offers to settle (rr 355, 358, 360-362)`

-- r 355(1): an offer must specify "a period, ending not less than 14 days after the day of service of the offer, during
-- which the offer is open for acceptance". The earliest lawful closing day.
GIVEN `the day the offer was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 355(1) -- the earliest closing day of an offer` `the day the offer was served` MEANS
    `the last day of n days after` `the day the offer was served` 14

-- r 355(1): an offer "may not be withdrawn during that period without the court's leave"; (2) it "lapses at the end of
-- the period". After the period there is nothing left to withdraw.
DECLARE `Withdrawal answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: not while it is open, without the court's leave`
    `yes, with the court's leave, though it can still be accepted until the application is decided`
    `there is nothing to withdraw: the offer lapsed at the end of its period`

GIVEN `the offer's closing day` IS A DATE, `the day I want to withdraw` IS A DATE, `the court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Withdrawal answer`
`r 355 -- can I withdraw my offer` `the offer's closing day` `the day I want to withdraw` `the court gives leave` MEANS
    IF `is after` `the day I want to withdraw` `the offer's closing day`
    THEN `there is nothing to withdraw: the offer lapsed at the end of its period`
    ELSE IF `the court gives leave`
         THEN `yes, with the court's leave, though it can still be accepted until the application is decided`
         ELSE `no: not while it is open, without the court's leave`

-- r 358(1): accepted "only by serving a written notice of acceptance on the party making the offer"; (2)-(3) a rejection
-- or counteroffer does not end it; r 355(2) lapse at the end of the period, (3) acceptance possible "at any time before
-- the application for leave to withdraw it is decided", (6) the court "may not ... extend the time for accepting an
-- offer". A period the text fixes: outside it, JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the offer's closing day` IS A DATE, `the day I serve my acceptance` IS A DATE,
      `the court gave leave to withdraw it before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`rr 355, 358 -- I can accept the offer` `the offer's closing day` `the day I serve my acceptance` `the court gave leave to withdraw it before that day` MEANS
    `yes or no`
        (    `is on or before` `the day I serve my acceptance` `the offer's closing day`
         AND (NOT `the court gave leave to withdraw it before that day`))

DECLARE `Who made the offer` IS ONE OF
    `I made the offer to the defendant`
    `the defendant made the offer to me`

DECLARE `Offer costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `the offer rules do not apply: costs are in the court's discretion and follow the event unless it orders otherwise (r 681)`
    `the court decides: the other side has shown another costs order is appropriate`
    `the defendant must pay my costs: standard basis up to and including the day the offer was served, indemnity basis after it (r 360)`
    `the defendant pays my standard costs up to and including the day of service; I pay its indemnity costs after it and get none of mine after it (r 361(2))`
    `I get standard costs to the opening of court on the next trial day; the defendant gets its indemnity costs after that (r 361(3))`
    `I must pay the defendant's costs: standard basis up to and including the day the offer was served, indemnity basis after it (r 361A)`

-- r 360 (my offer): not accepted, I obtain "an order no less favourable than the offer", and the court is satisfied I
-- was "at all material times willing and able to carry out" the offer; then "Unless the defendant shows another order
-- for costs is appropriate", standard to the day of service, indemnity after. r 361 (the defendant's offer): not
-- accepted, I obtain "an order that is less favourable to the plaintiff than the offer", the court is satisfied the
-- defendant was willing and able; (2) the split; (3) an offer served "on the first day or a later day of the trial". r
-- 361A: the defendant's offer, my proceeding dismissed. r 362: interest for the period after the day of service is
-- disregarded in comparing (asked so). Money offers are compared by amount: "no less favourable" is at least the
-- offer, "less favourable" is below it, so a judgment equal to the defendant's offer triggers neither r 361 nor
-- (unless I made the offer) anything (finding 4).
GIVEN `who made it` IS A `Who made the offer`, `the offer was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `my proceeding was dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the amount offered` IS A NUMBER,
      `the amount of my judgment` IS A NUMBER,
      `the court is satisfied the offeror was willing and able to carry it out` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the offer was served on or after the first day of the trial` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the other side shows another costs order is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Offer costs answer`
`rr 360-362 -- the costs consequence of the offer` `who made it` `the offer was accepted` `my proceeding was dismissed` `the amount offered` `the amount of my judgment` `the court is satisfied the offeror was willing and able to carry it out` `the offer was served on or after the first day of the trial` `the other side shows another costs order is appropriate` MEANS
    IF `the offer was accepted` OR (NOT `the court is satisfied the offeror was willing and able to carry it out`)
    THEN `the offer rules do not apply: costs are in the court's discretion and follow the event unless it orders otherwise (r 681)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `who made it`
         WHEN `I made the offer to the defendant` THEN
             IF (NOT `my proceeding was dismissed`) AND `the amount of my judgment` AT LEAST `the amount offered`
             THEN IF `the other side shows another costs order is appropriate`
                  THEN `the court decides: the other side has shown another costs order is appropriate`
                  ELSE `the defendant must pay my costs: standard basis up to and including the day the offer was served, indemnity basis after it (r 360)`
             ELSE `the offer rules do not apply: costs are in the court's discretion and follow the event unless it orders otherwise (r 681)`
         WHEN `the defendant made the offer to me` THEN
             IF `my proceeding was dismissed`
             THEN IF `the other side shows another costs order is appropriate`
                  THEN `the court decides: the other side has shown another costs order is appropriate`
                  ELSE `I must pay the defendant's costs: standard basis up to and including the day the offer was served, indemnity basis after it (r 361A)`
             ELSE IF `the amount of my judgment` LESS THAN `the amount offered`
                  THEN IF `the offer was served on or after the first day of the trial`
                       THEN `I get standard costs to the opening of court on the next trial day; the defendant gets its indemnity costs after that (r 361(3))`
                       ELSE IF `the other side shows another costs order is appropriate`
                            THEN `the court decides: the other side has shown another costs order is appropriate`
                            ELSE `the defendant pays my standard costs up to and including the day of service; I pay its indemnity costs after it and get none of mine after it (r 361(2))`
                  ELSE `the offer rules do not apply: costs are in the court's discretion and follow the event unless it orders otherwise (r 681)`

§§ `Chapter 10, Part 4 -- delay (r 389)`

DECLARE `Delay answer` IS ONE OF
    `no notice or order needed: a year has not passed without a step`
    `I must first give every other party a month's notice of my intention to proceed`
    `I need the court's order before taking a new step`

-- r 389: "(1) If no step has been taken in a proceeding for 1 year from the time the last step was taken, a party who
-- wants to proceed must, before taking any step in the proceeding, give a month's notice to every other party ... (2) If
-- no step has been taken ... for 2 years ..., a new step may not be taken without the order of the court". (3) An
-- application in which no order has been made is not a step (asked so). A year "from" the last step ends on its
-- anniversary; a step on the anniversary is within the year (fork F3).
GIVEN `the day the last step was taken` IS A DATE, `the day I want to take the next step` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Delay answer`
`r 389 -- what must I do before my next step` `the day the last step was taken` `the day I want to take the next step` MEANS
    IF `is after` `the day I want to take the next step` (`the nth anniversary of` `the day the last step was taken` 2)
    THEN `I need the court's order before taking a new step`
    ELSE IF `is after` `the day I want to take the next step` (`the nth anniversary of` `the day the last step was taken` 1)
         THEN `I must first give every other party a month's notice of my intention to proceed`
         ELSE `no notice or order needed: a year has not passed without a step`

-- r 389(1) "a month's notice": the month after the day the notice is given ends on the corresponding day of the next
-- month; the step can be taken on the day after (fork F4).
GIVEN `the day I gave notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 389(1) -- the first day I can take the step after notice` `the day I gave notice` MEANS
    `the day n days after` (`the same day n months later` `the day I gave notice` 1) 1

§§ `Chapter 13, Part 9 -- minor claims in a Magistrates Court (rr 514, 515)`

DECLARE `Simplified procedures answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is a minor claim, so the simplified procedures apply`
    `yes, to the extent the parties agreed in writing and filed the agreement`
    `no: the simplified procedures do not apply`

-- Schedule 3: "minor claim-- (a) means a claim for an amount, including interest, of not more than $25,000, whether as a
-- balance or after an admitted set-off, reduction by any amount paid by or credited to the defendant, abandonment of any
-- excess, or otherwise; but (b) does not include a claim for a liquidated demand mentioned in the QCAT Act, schedule 3,
-- definition minor civil dispute, paragraph 1(a)." r 514(1): the simplified procedures apply to minor claims; (2) to
-- another claim if the parties agree in writing and file the agreement; (3) but not for that QCAT liquidated demand.
-- A "means" definition: outside it, no.
GIVEN `the amount I claim, including interest, after set-offs, payments and any excess I abandon` IS A NUMBER,
      `it is a QCAT minor civil dispute liquidated demand` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the parties agreed in writing and filed the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Simplified procedures answer`
`rr 514, Schedule 3 -- do the simplified procedures apply` `the amount I claim, including interest, after set-offs, payments and any excess I abandon` `it is a QCAT minor civil dispute liquidated demand` `the parties agreed in writing and filed the agreement` MEANS
    IF `it is a QCAT minor civil dispute liquidated demand`
    THEN `no: the simplified procedures do not apply`
    ELSE IF `the amount I claim, including interest, after set-offs, payments and any excess I abandon` AT MOST 25000
         THEN `yes: it is a minor claim, so the simplified procedures apply`
         ELSE IF `the parties agreed in writing and filed the agreement`
              THEN `yes, to the extent the parties agreed in writing and filed the agreement`
              ELSE `no: the simplified procedures do not apply`

§§ `Chapter 17A -- costs (rr 691, 697, Schedule 2)`

DECLARE `Basis of costs` IS ONE OF `the standard basis`, `the indemnity basis`

DECLARE `Magistrates scale column` IS ONE OF
    `column A ($2,500 or under)`
    `column B (over $2,500 but not over $5,000)`
    `column C (over $5,000 but not over $20,000)`
    `column D (over $20,000 but not over $50,000)`
    `Part 3 (over $50,000)`

-- r 691(3): "For an assessment for Magistrates Courts on the standard basis, the scale in schedule 2 appropriate for
-- the amount the plaintiff recovers applies." (4): "on the indemnity basis, ... the amount the plaintiff claims".
-- Schedule 2, Part 2 columns A-D; Part 3 "applies if the amount recovered or claimed by the plaintiff is over $50,000".
GIVEN `the basis` IS A `Basis of costs`, `the amount I recovered` IS A NUMBER, `the amount I claimed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Magistrates scale column`
`r 691, Schedule 2 -- the Magistrates Courts scale column` `the basis` `the amount I recovered` `the amount I claimed` MEANS
    IF `the amount` AT MOST 2500
    THEN `column A ($2,500 or under)`
    ELSE IF `the amount` AT MOST 5000
         THEN `column B (over $2,500 but not over $5,000)`
         ELSE IF `the amount` AT MOST 20000
              THEN `column C (over $5,000 but not over $20,000)`
              ELSE IF `the amount` AT MOST 50000
                   THEN `column D (over $20,000 but not over $50,000)`
                   ELSE `Part 3 (over $50,000)`
    WHERE
        `the amount` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the basis`
            WHEN `the standard basis` THEN `the amount I recovered`
            WHEN `the indemnity basis` THEN `the amount I claimed`

DECLARE `Higher court costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `assessed as if the proceeding had been started in a Magistrates Court, unless the court orders otherwise`
    `assessed as if the proceeding had been started in the District Court, unless the court orders otherwise`
    `rule 697 does not reduce my costs`

-- r 697: (1)-(2) a judgment in the Supreme or District Court that "when the proceeding began, could have been given in
-- a Magistrates Court": costs "assessed as if the proceeding had been started in the Magistrates Court, unless the
-- court orders otherwise"; (3)-(4) the only relief in the Supreme Court could have been given by the District Court but
-- not a Magistrates Court: as if started in the District Court. The courts' limits are in their own Acts (not
-- deposited), asked.
GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`, `I sued in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a Magistrates Court could have given my judgment when I began` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the District Court could have given my relief when I began` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Higher court costs answer`
`r 697 -- are my costs cut back for suing in a higher court` `the court` `I sued in the Supreme Court` `a Magistrates Court could have given my judgment when I began` `the District Court could have given my relief when I began` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the court`
    WHEN `a Magistrates Court` THEN `rule 697 does not reduce my costs`
    WHEN `the Supreme Court or the District Court` THEN
        IF `a Magistrates Court could have given my judgment when I began`
        THEN `assessed as if the proceeding had been started in a Magistrates Court, unless the court orders otherwise`
        ELSE IF `I sued in the Supreme Court` AND `the District Court could have given my relief when I began`
             THEN `assessed as if the proceeding had been started in the District Court, unless the court orders otherwise`
             ELSE `rule 697 does not reduce my costs`

§§ `Chapter 18 -- appeals to the Court of Appeal (r 748)`

-- r 748: "A notice of appeal must, unless the Court of Appeal orders otherwise-- (a) be filed within 28 days after the
-- date of the decision appealed from; and (b) be served as soon as practicable on all other parties".
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 748 -- the last day to file my notice of appeal` `the day of the decision` MEANS
    `the last day of n days after` `the day of the decision` 28
